Size the collapsed bubble to its contents instead of guessing

The collapsed pill was pinned to a hardcoded 266 px, which is 18 px narrower
than the row of controls actually needs, so the Stop button was clipped by the
edge of the card. The number could only ever have been right for one state:
"Pause" becoming "Resume" needs 296, and a meeting past the hour mark grows the
timer to 01:23:45 and needs 318.

The renderer now measures the header - children, gaps, padding, card margin and
border - and asks for exactly that, re-fitting whenever the pause label or the
timer changes width, and once more after Geist finishes loading, since
measuring against the fallback font's metrics is another way to come up short.
Header items no longer shrink, so a squeezed button cannot make the measurement
lie about what fits.

build/test-bubble-fit.js opens the real bubble window and checks in all three
states that the row fits its header and that Stop lands inside the card.

